# the save journal: saves append to flash erased at power-on, so a save never pauses the sound. The
# journal's flash starts full of leftovers (the host emulates them); a power cut at any point of a save leaves
# the save before it; when the journal fills, a save falls back to OBJ_PROJ (a sector erase); the newest wins
wait 800
expect jr_erases >0
expect store_writes 0
# the instrument (HOME held), and a key to save: 1本 -> 2本
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
expect mode 0
turn SELECT 1 80
wait 100
expect par0 5
tap SAVE
wait 50
expect dirty 0
expect store_writes 0
reboot
wait 1500
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
expect par0 5
# a power cut on program 1 of the next save (the project in five 64-byte pieces, then the commit): the save before stays
turn SELECT 1 80
wait 100
expect par0 6
jrtear 1
tap SAVE
wait 50
reboot
wait 1500
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
expect par0 5
# a power cut on program 2 of the next save (the project in five 64-byte pieces, then the commit): the save before stays
turn SELECT 1 80
wait 100
expect par0 6
jrtear 2
tap SAVE
wait 50
reboot
wait 1500
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
expect par0 5
# a power cut on program 3 of the next save (the project in five 64-byte pieces, then the commit): the save before stays
turn SELECT 1 80
wait 100
expect par0 6
jrtear 3
tap SAVE
wait 50
reboot
wait 1500
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 100
expect par0 5
# a power cut on program 4 of the next save (the project in five 64-byte pieces, then the commit): the save before stays
